  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given nnn numbers a1,a2,...ana_1,a_2, ... a_na1​,a2​,...an​ and another number xxx. Let P=p1,p2,...pnP= p_1,p_2,...p_nP=p1​,p2​,...pn​ be any permutation of  1,2,...n1,2,...n1,2,...n.\n\nYour task is to find the number of distinct values of ((((x%ap1)%ap2)%ap3...)%apn((((x\\%a_{p_1})\\%a_{p_2})\\%a_{p_3}...)\\%a_{p_n}((((x%ap1​​)%ap2​​)%ap3​​...)%apn​​\n\nInput:\nThe first line contains TTT, the number of testcases.\nThere are two lines in each testcase. The first line contains the numbers nnn and xxx.\nThe second line contains the nnn numbers a1,a2,...ana_1,a_2,...a_na1​,a2​,...an​ separated by spaces.\nOutput:Output in a single line the number of distinct values.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤n≤1051 \\leq n \\leq 10^51≤n≤105",
      "1≤x≤1091 \\leq x \\leq 10^91≤x≤109",
      "1≤ai≤1051 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^51≤ai​≤105",
      "The sum of nnn over all testcases doesn't exceed 10510^5105.",
      "Sample Input:`1",
      "2 5",
      "2 3",
      "`Sample Output:`2",
      "`EXPLANATION:(5%2)%3=1(5\\%2)\\%3 = 1(5%2)%3=1",
      "(5%3)%2=0(5\\%3)\\%2 = 0(5%3)%2=0",
      "Thus there are 2 distinct numbers."
    ],
